# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# IDE files
/.idea

# Rust
/target
# dist/ is build output and stays ignored. sp-server's build.rs creates the
# directory rust-embed needs at compile time, so nothing has to be tracked here
# — a placeholder file would not survive, since trunk wipes dist/ on every build.
dist/

# The user's global ~/.gitignore excludes `.cargo`, but sp-web-host's .cargo/config.toml
# carries the rustflags that make `trunk build` produce a wasm-opt-valid module. Without it
# tracked, the browser build fails on a fresh clone.
!crates/sp-web-host/.cargo/

# Same reasoning: the root .cargo/config.toml carries the `cargo xtask` alias.
!/.cargo/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
.playwright-cli/
